      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/McConnellstown%2C_Pennsylvania"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The community lies in Woodcock Valley, bordered by Crooked Creek, a tributary of the Juniata River.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/McConnellstown%2C_Pennsylvania"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Pennsylvania Route 26 runs through McConnellstown, leading 5 miles northeast to Huntingdon and 7 miles southwest to Marklesburg.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        24
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/McConnellstown%2C_Pennsylvania"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Between 1850 and about 1895, Pennsylvania Railroad tracks ran along Allegheny Street, bringing trains into town.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
